Advanced causal dispersive pulse study (@em-dispersion-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1", #source "../sources/Electromagnetics-and-Applications-Staelin.lingua#r_45QC1TW6RXJBJE8Q5H98DZT5AC", #source "../sources/Measuring-Permittivity-and-Permeability-NIST-TN-1536.lingua#r_6BH70T5QSNJ7P7RKZ0G133CM91", #electromagnetism "../study/An-integrated-electromagnetic-system-investigation.lingua#r_1FQW2ASX2WCT3JRXKKP4NB4HSN") { r_2JT83809PYYT57JSB8JGW8QPBK
**Read:** [Electromagnetism — David Tong](../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1), complete dispersive-matter and wave development; [Electromagnetics and Applications — David H. Staelin](../sources/Electromagnetics-and-Applications-Staelin.lingua#r_45QC1TW6RXJBJE8Q5H98DZT5AC), whole pulse/dispersion treatment; [Measuring Permittivity and Permeability — NIST TN 1536](../sources/Measuring-Permittivity-and-Permeability-NIST-TN-1536.lingua#r_6BH70T5QSNJ7P7RKZ0G133CM91), applicable complete material methods.

Choose a passive dispersive model with a clear microscopic/effective interpretation. Read the complete response, causality and wave chapters of [Electromagnetism — David Tong](../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1), [Classical Electromagnetism — Richard Fitzpatrick](../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H) and the relevant [Electromagnetics and Applications — David H. Staelin](../sources/Electromagnetics-and-Applications-Staelin.lingua#r_45QC1TW6RXJBJE8Q5H98DZT5AC) development; compare with [Measuring Permittivity and Permeability — NIST TN 1536](../sources/Measuring-Permittivity-and-Permeability-NIST-TN-1536.lingua#r_6BH70T5QSNJ7P7RKZ0G133CM91) where material data are used. Derive the time-domain kernel and frequency-domain response from the same equations.

Propagate a finite-band pulse through a finite sample, including interfaces. Compare harmonic transfer, a time-domain calculation and limiting analytical results. Track input/output energy, absorption, reshaping and material storage. Distinguish phase delay, envelope/group delay, energy flow and causal-front claims. Test what changes when the pulse is too broadband for a quadratic expansion of k(ω).

Fit or choose parameters under stated passivity and stability conditions, then examine uncertainty from unmeasured spectral tails. Demonstrate a deliberately misleading peak-velocity interpretation and explain it through the full input/output signal. Verify causality and asymptotes rather than extrapolating a narrow-band fit without limits. The result should give a physically consistent account of a pulse and specimen, with convergence and material-model uncertainty kept separate.

**Continue:** [An integrated electromagnetic-system investigation](../study/An-integrated-electromagnetic-system-investigation.lingua#r_1FQW2ASX2WCT3JRXKKP4NB4HSN).

**Return:** [Electromagnetism — charge, fields, matter, waves and physical evidence](../Electromagnetism.lingua#r_5TJPESCTTNAKY66JH2QNQYN1PY).
